    "notes": "1. 'total_operating_cost' includes Cost of sales, Marketing and selling expenses, General and administrative expenses, and Other operating income and expenses (which is a net expense). This aligns with standard practice for a luxury goods conglomerate where operating costs encompass all costs directly tied to operations before financing and taxes. 2. 'interest_expenses' includes Cost of net financial debt, Interest on lease liabilities, and Other financial income and expenses. Per rule 13, the sign for 'Other financial income and expenses' is reversed (positive in the statement becomes negative here) because it was net income that increases profit; as an expense component, we report it as a negative value (i.e., a reduction to the interest expense total). 3. 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is not included in total_operating_cost as it is non-operating income. 4. All numbers from the primary statement have been used. Parentheses in the source indicate negative values, which have been converted to positive numbers for cost and expense fields per rule 13.",
